bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_import_alias_resolves_to_colliding_global_fn_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (seed 1c781f0f8d6fb1c3, release/1.0.0 669f7aabbe9, aarch64): with `use std.websocket.handshake.{ws_handshake_text_to_bytes as text_to_bytes}`, `val p = text_to_bytes("ab")` is typed [u8] (the signature of the unrelated global std text_to_bytes in common/base_encoding.spl) instead of List<i64>, so passing p to a [i64] parameter raises E1003 under compile and strict JIT; the unaliased call `ws_handshake_text_to_bytes("ab")` types as List<i64> and runs (98). Seen in src/lib/nogc_async_mut/websocket/upgrade.spl write_frame; worked around there by calling the unaliased name. Same alias form remains in websocket frame.spl, message.spl, utilities.spl, connection.spl. Fixture: scratch alias_alias.spl / alias_plain.spl in the E1003 lane."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    seed_import_alias_resolves_to_colliding_global_fn_2026-11-27, P2, open, "Seed: an import alias that shares a name with another stdlib fn resolves calls (and their return type) to that other fn", src/lib/nogc_async_mut/websocket/upgrade.spl, 21, NONE, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

